  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 103 AM MDT Tue Sep 15 2026\n\nChilly start to the morning with many areas falling into the \n30s. The frost advisory remains in effect until 9am. Temps \nshould quickly rebound with most locations seeing highs in the \n70s today. Overnight lows look like they'll stay warm enough in \nmost locations for Wednesday morning. Although there could be a \nfew spots across the upper Snake Plain that could see some \npatchy frost. Temps rise to near 80 in across most of the Snake \nPlain and eastern Magic Valley on Wednesday. Meanwhile, a low \npressure system will work into the Pacific Northwest. This \nsystem will lift monsoonal moisture into our region for \nWednesday through Friday resulting in showers and storms. The \nlow will pass through over the weekend and potentially we could \nsee another round of frost advisories for Saturday and Sunday \nmornings.",
